# grammar.md 4.2: a line terminator inside an interpolation ends both the
# interpolation and the string. The newline is a code-mode Newline; on the
# next line `}` is RBrace and the `"` starts a new unterminated string.
LetKw "let"
Ident "s"
Eq "="
StringStart "\""
InterpStart "{"
Ident "a"
Newline "\n"
Ident "b"
RBrace "}"
StringStart "\""
Newline "\n"
